From 61b131802303d83f917a4445cf9d446a4b2faef9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:31:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 92/93] blitz-dom: date and time inputs are one-line fields
 showing their value

A date, time, datetime-local, month or week input had no editor, so it was
laid out with no content and drew nothing: only its border and padding
showed. Blitz has no picker for these types, so lay each out as a one-line
text field showing its value as HTML gives it (ISO 8601, which needs no
locale), sanitized as HTML sanitizes it (a string that is not a valid one of
the type's is empty), and, while it is empty, its format as the placeholder.
It is as wide as its format and a character more; `size` is not its. Form
submission sends the field's text once it is a valid value, and nothing
before.
